From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui.xaml: pointer input -- buttons are clicked

NanaZip's toolbar drew but did not respond. A XAML host window now hit-tests the mouse against its content -- the topmost visible, hit-testable element under the pointer, its nearest button -- shows the pointer over a button and its press, and clicks the button when the mouse button is released over the one pressed (ClickMode Release): its Click handlers (RoutedEventHandler, the button as sender, RoutedEventArgs) and its Command (ICommand CanExecute/Execute). A press released elsewhere clicks nothing. Markup also converts CommandBar label positions, overflow-button visibility and ClickMode by name. The implementation is ours. Behind the XAML switch of 6131.
---
